## The recurring findings on this track, and what each one measures
Do not re-explain the problem back — change the thing the finding measures.  If a measured
finding repeats from the previous round, re-read its number and change what it measures until
the number passes; a judge note that repeats needs a visible change in the named view.

| what the judge or gate wrote | the requirement behind it |
|---|---|
| flat / one-colour ground, no paths, hard raised-bed edges | the surface needs visible variation that matches the brief (material, relief, wear) where the setting would show it (judge `flat_ground`) |
| a hard world edge against the sky, missing horizon | from no camera may the ground end against the sky (`world_edge_visible`; the gate reads standing geometry to 1.25 × the bounds half-extent, fog far ≥ 2 × the plan span); what continues the world is the brief's — the street keeps going, the sea, a cliff, a forest, a city, a wall, or fog that closes |
| the backdrop looks like flat / beige / untextured cut-outs | distant forms need volume and shading consistent with the sky's light (judge `placeholder_material`); aerial perspective comes from the fog, not from pre-tinting the material toward it |
| a pond / terrace is a hard-edged plane sitting on the ground | a water body or terrace must meet the ground without a visible hard seam (judge); carving the terrain or dressing the edge are two options |
| "camera is N m below ground level" | the eye must be ≥ 0.3 m above the ground under it: compute the camera's y from `heightAt(x, z)` (or the floor it stands on) in `src/scene.js` |
| identical cones / stacked blocks / primitive repetition | the judge reads identical copies and primitive stacks; vary silhouette, scale and colour where the brief has natural variety (a planted avenue or a container stack IS regular — the brief decides) |
| sparse, token, "a diorama on a plane", empty midground | the description's contents are requirements (the census compares them: `missing_content`, `zone_empty`; a count under half the layout's is an INFO `density_note`); "sparse / diorama" means the frame has empty regions the brief would fill — fill them with what the brief implies |
| flat / dark / monochrome light, black shade, jagged shadows | flat / dark frames are measured (mean lum, std, flat band); jagged shadows mean shadow texels larger than ~0.05 m over the content — tighten the frustum (`sunRig({ bounds })` with the content radius); the light's colours are the brief's time of day and sources |
| frames at t=0 and t=1.5 identical, "nothing moves", `no_motion` | a camera moves when ≥ 0.4 % of its pixels change by more than 8/255 (or ≥ 0.08 % by more than 60/255); none moving is the gate's `no_motion` ERROR and the judge's `nothing_moves`; the hook is `userData.update` (never `tick`), and the amplitude has to show at 1024×576 (foliage ±0.10–0.20 rad, particles ≥ 0.6 m per 1.5 s, water ≥ 3 cm or a scrolling normal are amplitudes that have passed) |
| `hard_edged_particles`, "sharp-edged quads / spheres / discs for steam, dust, sparks", the brief's "soft particle effect" must-item unverified | the finding measures sharp-edged particle sprites; any soft-edged construction passes (the library's `makeSmoke` / `makeSteam` / `makeMotes` / `makeFire` volumes, or a radial-alpha sprite on every point) |
| camera inside geometry / shows only sky or a wall | the eye must be ≥ 0.5 m from every surface and the frame ≥ 10 % content (20 % for the establishing view): move the camera in `src/scene.js` or what blocks it |
